From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 16:58:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] EXCPT: 68000 exceptions reported by a BricoExt ROM

The Brico68k exception handlers send the 68k command EXCPT (vector, SR,
PC, access address) then EOT, instead of plain text:
- idle: HandleCommands runs it like PRTXT;
- during an extension: CommandExtension shows the output sent before the
  exception as usual (InputBuffer read limit), then runs the report and
  returns "[Extension aborted by a 68000 exception]" (stops a loop).

Only syntax-checked on a PC (g++ with stub SDK headers): not built with the
Pico SDK, not run on a BricoNeo.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01A4z9PLhKHyqQSeWRabEyo9
